[1;34m"body"[m[1;38m:[m [32m"![medium](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/medium-priority.svg)\n\nCurrently, `this.mesh` is a `THREE.Mesh` representing the enemy cone, and the health bars are added as its children. Since `this.mesh` rotates in the `update` loop, the health bars (which are children of `this.mesh`) also rotate in world space, which breaks the billboard effect (they won't face the camera correctly). To fix this, make `this.mesh` a `THREE.Group` and add a separate visual mesh (e.g., `this.cone`) to it. This allows you to rotate only the visual mesh while keeping the parent group (and the health bars) unrotated.\n\n```javascript\n    createMesh() {\n        this.mesh = new THREE.Group();\n        this.mesh.position.copy(this.path[0]);\n        this.mesh.position.y = 7.5;\n\n        this.cone = new THREE.Mesh(enemyGeometry, enemyMaterial);\n        this.mesh.add(this.cone);\n\n        this.scene.add(this.mesh);\n\n        this.createHealthBar();\n    }\n```"[m[1;38m,[m
